// AI Gateway Private — Log Analytics queries
//
// Workspace : log-aigwp-csmgv3poae57c  (rg-ai-gateway-private)
// Portal    : Log Analytics workspaces > log-aigwp-csmgv3poae57c > Logs
//   or      : API Management > aigwp-apim-csmgv3poae57c > Monitoring > Logs
//
// NOTE: the time-range picker in the portal overrides any ago() filter below.
// If a query returns nothing, check the picker before assuming logging is broken.
//
// NOTE: these queries use the resource-specific table ApiManagementGatewayLogs,
// which only receives data because the diagnostic setting sets
// logAnalyticsDestinationType: 'Dedicated' (see modules/observability.bicep).
// Without it, rows land in the legacy AzureDiagnostics table instead and this
// table stays permanently empty — indistinguishable from logging being broken.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. THE PROOF — did agent egress move inside the VNet?
//
// Every request the prompt agent makes to the model passes through APIM, so
// CallerIpAddress is the agent's source address.
//   51.12.x.x  = Microsoft's network, egress left your VNet
//   10.20.1.x  = the data proxy NIC inside snet-agent
//
// Measured on this lab:
//   BEFORE stage 7 : 2026-09-16 08:25:24 UTC  51.12.146.124  200
//   AFTER  stage 7 : 2026-09-16 09:34:36 UTC  10.20.1.14     200
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ApiManagementGatewayLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| extend Path = iff(CallerIpAddress startswith "10.", "PRIVATE (snet-agent)", "PUBLIC (internet)")
| project TimeGenerated, Path, CallerIpAddress, ResponseCode, BackendResponseCode, Url
| order by TimeGenerated asc


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Raw gateway traffic
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ApiManagementGatewayLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| project TimeGenerated, CallerIpAddress, Method, Url, ResponseCode, BackendResponseCode, IsRequestSuccess
| order by TimeGenerated desc


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Who is still reaching the PUBLIC gateway?
//
// Run this before and after setting allowPublicGatewayAccess: false.
// Expect Microsoft Defender for Cloud probing /mdcscanner from an fd00::/8
// address roughly every 2 hours — harmless, but live evidence the public
// listener is still open. After the door is closed these should stop.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ApiManagementGatewayLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where not(CallerIpAddress startswith "10.")
| summarize Requests = count(), Last = max(TimeGenerated) by CallerIpAddress, Url, ResponseCode
| order by Last desc


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 4. Model and token detail (AI-gateway specific table)
//
// Table name is ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog — singular "Log", unlike
// ApiManagementGatewayLogs. This is what makes it an *AI* gateway rather than
// a plain reverse proxy: per-request model and token counts, the basis for
// chargeback and for token-limit policies.
//
// Run `ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog | getschema` first — column names vary by
// API version and were not verified on this workspace.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| take 20


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5. Errors only
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ApiManagementGatewayLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where ResponseCode >= 400
| project TimeGenerated, CallerIpAddress, Url, ResponseCode, BackendResponseCode, LastErrorReason, LastErrorMessage
| order by TimeGenerated desc


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 6. Legacy fallback
//
// If the queries above are empty but the APIM "Requests" metric shows traffic,
// the diagnostic setting has reverted to the legacy shared table. Check here
// before concluding logging is broken. Column names differ: CallerIPAddress
// (capital IP) and typed suffixes such as responseCode_d, url_s.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AzureDiagnostics
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.APIMANAGEMENT"
| project TimeGenerated, CallerIPAddress, url_s, responseCode_d
| order by TimeGenerated desc
